  "question": {
    "text": "A ray of light is incident at an angle of incidence <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> on the glass slab of refractive index <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math>. After refraction, the light ray emerges out from other parallel faces and lateral shift between incident ray and emergent ray is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. The thickness of the glass slab is _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cm</mi></math>.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "12",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/46d4981a-0b63-4e98-8511-e6a57840e121-image.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 245px;\" /></p><p>From snell&#39;s law,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p><p>From the diagram shown,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math></p>",
